cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use XenoLog, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "XenoLog: a phone-based tool for priming records, rest periods and photo-assisted identification in Xenopus laevis colonies"
abstract: >-
  XenoLog is a phone web app for Xenopus laevis colonies. It records which
  female was primed and when, enforces a rest period between primings,
  collects the egg record on the day of collection, and keeps photos of each
  frog's back. A photo taken at the bench is matched in the browser against
  earlier photos of the frogs in the same housing tank (ORB keypoints with
  geometric verification, OpenCV.js); the match is a suggestion that a person
  confirms. It runs as a Google Apps Script web app bound to a spreadsheet,
  with no server to maintain.
authors:
  - given-names: Gembu
    family-names: Maryu
repository-code: "https://github.com/gmaryu/xenolog"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - Xenopus laevis
  - colony management
  - animal welfare
  - individual identification
  - dorsal pattern
  - laboratory records
  - Google Apps Script
  - OpenCV.js
